## Navigation

**`bench/idma_composition.c`** — standalone CLI, one `IDMA_IOC_RUN_COMPOSITION` (0x11) ioctl per run.
- Options: `--device` (default `/dev/idma0`), `--mode 0..3`, `--a-pages 0/1/8/16`, `--v-gap 0/1000/4000`, `--transfers 1..4096`, `--warmup 0..4096`, `--timeout-ms` (default 15000); `--help` and `--abi` short-circuit before any `open()`.
- `parse_u64` rejects sign/whitespace/overflow/trailing junk (strict `strtoull`); duplicate and unknown options rejected via a `seen` bitmask.
- `protected_did` hard-fixed to 10; aggressor is instance 1 / DID 11 or `NO_AGGRESSOR`; `p4m.aggressor_gap_cycles` fixed 0. (Solo keeps `aggressor_pages=1` — an assumption, noted in the source.)
- Output: one line `schema=idma-composition-v1` with `request`, `errno`, `result{status,restore_status,configured,raw_captured,generation,restored_generation,experiment{...victim/aggressor + hpm_field_semantics:"raw_only"},p4m{sequence,observer_status,observation[35],window[16]},raw[128]}`, plus `semantics`. Failure still emits JSON and returns non-zero. No rerun, no `/dev/mem`.
- Uses `PRIu64` with explicit `(uint64_t)`/`(unsigned int)` casts; `report()` uses a separate `int a` for `argc` and `unsigned int i` for the array loops so `-Wall -Wextra` stays clean.

**`scripts/composition_plan.py`** — import-only, stdlib only.
- `PLAN_GENERATION=1`, schemas, mode/raw-offset constants, `expected_live_config(mode)`.
- `build_plan()` → 172 cases in original order: 16 short (`4 mode × a0/1/8/16`, transfer16/warm16/gap0), 12 noise (`S/S6` pairs, a8/gap0/4096/256), 144 explore (`3 block × 3 gap × 4 a × 4 mode`, Latin rotation so S is not always first). Each case carries unique `id/phase/block/pair/slot/mode/a_pages/v_gap_cycles/transfers/warmup/timeout_ms/auto_rerun=False`; plan has `auto_rerun=False`, `resume=False`.
- `cases_through_phase`, `case_argv`, `validate_case(case, record, meta=None)`, `case_metrics`.
- Validator checks: schema/success/errno, request echo vs case params, composition ABI/status/restore/generation advance, raw[0] magic, raw[1] ABI, raw[2]/raw[10] live/frozen config, raw[3]/raw[11] generation frozen, raw[6] frozen bit, raw[8] cycles equal to `p4m.window[1]` (same window), raw[9] err0, raw[33]==0, V/A/other lookup conservation, Vgap/A-gap consistency, N-disabled fast>0 rejected (fast==0 never a failure), V workload counts, Solo/aggressor `has_a`, experiment/victim/aggressor data errors, and `meta` exit/taint. `case_metrics` uses `window[3]` (A completed in window, not the whole round), `transfers*4096` V bytes and 50 MHz/20 ns.

**`scripts/mac_composition.py`** — attach-only runner.
- Reuses `mac_research2.SerialConsole` (explicit API check: `start/close/run_shell/drain_input/disable_echo`); no dependency on the old `00093` gate.
- CLI: `--serial` (default `/dev/cu.usbserial-AV0KRCHT`), `--out`, required `--expected-kernel`, `--board-cli`, `--device`, `--plan`, `--run`, `--through-phase short/noise/explore` (default short), timeouts.
- `--plan` or absence of `--run` → writes `plan.json` + `manifest.json` and exits without opening serial. `--run` → lsof read-only exclusivity check, then finally-closes the console.
- Writes full plan before execution; per phase: cases → `dmesg.<phase>.end.txt` → phase count log → summary. Attach identity = `uname -r` (checked against `--expected-kernel`), boot_id, taint, `--abi` JSON. Per case: one framed CLI command capturing stdout JSON + exit + `taint.after`/`boot.after`; saves raw stdout, record, stderr, taint, meta; failure → `STOPPED.txt` and non-zero. No tar/base64/hash readback, no resume, no rerun. No hardcoded kernel value.

**`tests/test_composition_plan.py`** — stdlib `unittest`; loads `composition_plan.py` by path.
- Plan: 172 total, 16/12/144, unique ids, preserved phase order, short/noise/explore shapes, Latin rotation (each mode leads at least once, every group is a permutation), no auto-rerun, `case_argv`, `cases_through_phase`.
- Validator: valid solo/aggressor/gap records pass; taint, exit code, wrong window cycles, bad magic, wrong config, negative request param, broken lookup conservation, gap0 inconsistency, non-advancing generation, fast-while-N-disabled all fail; scientific `fast==0` and `miss==0` do not fail.

## Assumptions / unresolved
- **Solo `aggressor_pages=1`** and **`protected_did` encoding `(DID<<8)|mode` in raw[2]/raw[10]** are my reading of the spec (line 10) and the C tool echo; if the driver stores DID differently, adjust the C `build_request` and `expected_live_config`.
